WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.167 --> 00:00:02.628
Money Heist's fifth
and final season has begun

00:00:02.711 --> 00:00:04.671
and it really has
raised the roof.

00:00:04.755 --> 00:00:06.423
Well, technically
it dropped the roof

00:00:06.507 --> 00:00:08.425
with explosions
and all-out warfare

00:00:08.509 --> 00:00:09.843
seizing the Bank of Spain.

00:00:09.927 --> 00:00:11.428
Money Heist has always been

00:00:11.512 --> 00:00:13.347
a difficult show
to second-guess.

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.557
Would you ever have
predicted Arturo

00:00:15.641 --> 00:00:17.643
going full-Rambo
in a forklift truck?

00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:19.311
Yes, that happened.

00:00:20.103 --> 00:00:21.605
The wait now begins
for the final episodes

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:22.773
on December 3rd,

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:25.567
and it has left fans
wondering what lies in store

00:00:25.651 --> 00:00:26.944
for The Professor
and the gang.

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:29.655
So, let's round up
the juiciest fan theories

00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:31.823
about what might happen
in the final part

00:00:31.907 --> 00:00:33.075
of Money Heist.

00:00:33.158 --> 00:00:35.202
Do be careful
if you aren't up to date,

00:00:35.285 --> 00:00:36.411
there are
plenty of spoilers!

00:00:40.457 --> 00:00:43.877
The first half of Part 5
ended with a massive shock,

00:00:43.961 --> 00:00:45.879
as a wounded Tokyo
made a brave last stand

00:00:45.963 --> 00:00:48.966
against the special forces
and sacrificed herself

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.843
to give bald terminator
Gandía

00:00:50.926 --> 00:00:52.344
an explosive farewell.

00:00:55.764 --> 00:00:58.183
As the first character
we ever met in Money Heist,

00:00:58.267 --> 00:01:00.811
saying goodbye to Tokyo
was never going to be easy,

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:02.104
which maybe explains

00:01:02.187 --> 00:01:03.689
why some fans
are holding out hope

00:01:03.772 --> 00:01:05.274
that she isn't really dead.

00:01:05.357 --> 00:01:07.109
The main thinking
behind this theory

00:01:07.192 --> 00:01:08.861
is that Tokyo
is the show's narrator,

00:01:08.944 --> 00:01:10.404
and many believe
she's retelling

00:01:10.487 --> 00:01:12.197
the story of the heist
having survived it.

00:01:12.781 --> 00:01:14.741
Some even speculate
she's telling the story

00:01:14.825 --> 00:01:16.410
to Nairobi's son, Axel,

00:01:16.493 --> 00:01:18.161
to explain
how his mother died.

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:21.248
An even wilder theory

00:01:21.331 --> 00:01:22.958
is that the entire
Money Heist story

00:01:23.041 --> 00:01:24.668
is being made up
in Tokyo's head

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.628
and that it's actually
her way of coping

00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:28.338
with the tragedy
of losing her boyfriend

00:01:28.422 --> 00:01:30.799
in the first bank heist
we see in flashback.

00:01:30.883 --> 00:01:33.677
If either of these
narrator ideas were true,

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.138
Tokyo would need to be alive
to tell the tale.

00:01:36.221 --> 00:01:38.682
There's also the popular
fan theory from Part 4

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:41.768
that when Nairobi dies
she enters heaven or limbo

00:01:41.852 --> 00:01:43.854
and joins all the robbers
who've previously died:

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.856
Oslo, Moscow and Berlin.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:47.941
But earlier
in that same setting,

00:01:48.025 --> 00:01:50.819
we also see Denver,
The Professor and Helsinki,

00:01:50.903 --> 00:01:52.654
which could foreshadow
their deaths.

00:01:52.738 --> 00:01:54.781
Tokyo isn't seen
in this heavenly garden,

00:01:54.865 --> 00:01:56.950
so could it mean
she survives?

00:01:57.034 --> 00:01:58.785
Stacked up against
this theory is the fact

00:01:58.869 --> 00:02:01.163
that in Money Heist's
"Making Of" documentary

00:02:01.246 --> 00:02:02.623
From Tokyo to Berlin,

00:02:02.706 --> 00:02:04.958
we clearly see Tokyo actress
Úrsula Corberó

00:02:05.042 --> 00:02:07.878
give an emotional farewell
to the cast and crew.

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.588
If they faked
that to trick us,

00:02:09.671 --> 00:02:11.965
it would be a deception
worthy of The Professor.

00:02:12.049 --> 00:02:14.510
But, hey,
keep the dream alive, right?

00:02:14.593 --> 00:02:17.137
While the bank robbers have
a rough time in Part 5,

00:02:17.221 --> 00:02:18.931
Berlin has a much
smoother ride

00:02:19.014 --> 00:02:20.599
in flashbacks
to an earlier heist

00:02:20.682 --> 00:02:22.392
he pulled off in Copenhagen.

00:02:22.476 --> 00:02:23.435
The only explosion here

00:02:23.519 --> 00:02:25.354
was the popping
of champagne corks.

00:02:25.437 --> 00:02:28.690
These flashbacks reunite us
with Berlin's wife, Tatiana,

00:02:28.774 --> 00:02:31.151
and introduce his son,
Rafael.

00:02:31.235 --> 00:02:32.945
As neither Tatiana or Rafael

00:02:33.028 --> 00:02:34.863
have appeared
in the Bank of Spain heist,

00:02:34.947 --> 00:02:36.240
it has fans wondering

00:02:36.323 --> 00:02:38.867
if these two have a role to
play in the current robbery.

00:02:38.951 --> 00:02:40.786
As Berlin had been planning
the Bank of Spain job

00:02:40.869 --> 00:02:41.703
for many years,

00:02:41.787 --> 00:02:43.872
it might not be
a coincidence that his son

00:02:43.956 --> 00:02:46.834
ended up learning a skill
that could play a part.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:01.849
His whole education
just to prepare him

00:03:01.932 --> 00:03:03.267
to crack open banks,

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:05.561
and you thought
your parents were pushy.

00:03:05.644 --> 00:03:06.979
Another theory
is that Rafael

00:03:07.062 --> 00:03:09.439
is destined to team up
with Tatiana,

00:03:09.523 --> 00:03:11.859
potentially having an affair
with his dad's new wife.

00:03:11.942 --> 00:03:14.319
After all,
as Berlin explains to him…

00:03:14.403 --> 00:03:16.697
If you really want something
in life,

00:03:18.115 --> 00:03:20.200
you have to steal
it from whomever has it.

00:03:20.284 --> 00:03:21.618
And the look
on Rafael's face

00:03:21.702 --> 00:03:23.704
suggests
he has something in mind.

00:03:23.787 --> 00:03:25.664
If he were to team up
with Tatiana,

00:03:25.747 --> 00:03:26.915
could they throw a spanner

00:03:26.999 --> 00:03:28.917
in the works
of The Professor's plans?

00:03:29.001 --> 00:03:30.627
Fans theorised
back in Part 3

00:03:30.711 --> 00:03:33.297
that letting Tatiana in
on the Bank of Spain plan

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:34.631
was a bad idea.

00:03:34.715 --> 00:03:37.759
By the way, she loves the
Bank of Spain heist.

00:03:39.344 --> 00:03:40.304
She knows.

00:03:40.387 --> 00:03:42.347
Could she sweep in
with Rafael

00:03:42.431 --> 00:03:44.683
to take the prize
at the last moment?

00:03:44.766 --> 00:03:45.851
Time will tell.

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:47.352
However,
there's another theory

00:03:47.436 --> 00:03:48.520
which could take Money Heist

00:03:48.604 --> 00:03:50.230
in a very different
direction.

00:03:50.314 --> 00:03:51.857
Some fans think Rafael

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.650
is actually
The Professor's son.

00:03:53.734 --> 00:03:54.651
With his glasses

00:03:54.735 --> 00:03:56.445
and slightly awkward
social skills,

00:03:56.528 --> 00:03:57.946
he certainly
has more in common

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:00.866
with the brainy mastermind
than suave Berlin.

00:04:00.949 --> 00:04:02.409
This would also
provide an answer

00:04:02.492 --> 00:04:04.745
to one of the biggest
mysteries of Part 5.

00:04:04.828 --> 00:04:06.955
When Alicia Sierra
is interrogating

00:04:07.039 --> 00:04:08.582
the captured Professor
in his lair,

00:04:08.665 --> 00:04:11.502
she accuses him of lying
to his brother, Berlin.

00:04:11.585 --> 00:04:14.546
I'm trying to set the facts
straight and tell the truth.

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:16.256
You've been lying
the whole time.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:18.592
You didn't even tell
your brother the truth.

00:04:18.675 --> 00:04:20.552
What truth
is she referring to?

00:04:20.636 --> 00:04:22.596
If The Professor
was Rafael's dad,

00:04:22.679 --> 00:04:24.181
that would be
a pretty big secret

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:25.432
between the brothers.

00:04:25.516 --> 00:04:27.267
Or maybe
it's just more mind games

00:04:27.351 --> 00:04:28.977
from the devious Alicia.

00:04:29.061 --> 00:04:30.229
Speaking of Alicia,

00:04:30.312 --> 00:04:31.647
the interrogator
we love to hate

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:33.273
has lots of fans
guessing about

00:04:33.357 --> 00:04:35.400
whether she can be trusted
going forwards.

00:04:35.484 --> 00:04:37.194
You'd think that
The Professor helping her

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:38.320
during a traumatic birth

00:04:38.403 --> 00:04:39.488
would bond them for life,

00:04:39.571 --> 00:04:42.824
but careful viewers don't
believe she's on Team Heist.

00:04:43.325 --> 00:04:45.202
For starters, she was
clearly seen hiding

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:46.954
a pair of pliers
up her sleeve.

00:04:47.037 --> 00:04:48.413
Now, she could just
be planning

00:04:48.497 --> 00:04:50.541
to help Marseille
put together that crib,

00:04:50.624 --> 00:04:51.917
but fans think
she's planning

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.795
to cut The Professor's
communication with the bank.

00:04:54.878 --> 00:04:56.296
Eagle-eyed viewers
also point out

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:57.464
a moment during the birth

00:04:57.548 --> 00:04:59.341
where Alicia
is clearly seen reading

00:04:59.424 --> 00:05:00.551
The Professor's documents

00:05:00.634 --> 00:05:02.135
as she searches
for equipment.

00:05:02.219 --> 00:05:03.762
Could it be
that she's figured out

00:05:03.846 --> 00:05:04.805
The Professor's plan

00:05:04.888 --> 00:05:06.306
and is working
to double-cross him?

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:07.891
If Alicia
can't trust the robbers

00:05:07.975 --> 00:05:09.393
or her former friends
with the police,

00:05:09.476 --> 00:05:12.479
she might try
taking the gold for herself.

00:05:12.563 --> 00:05:13.814
One thing's for sure,

00:05:13.897 --> 00:05:16.066
never underestimate
Alicia Sierra,

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:17.901
as she warns
The Professor herself.

00:05:17.985 --> 00:05:20.320
There are no big battles
without big opponents.

00:05:20.404 --> 00:05:21.822
Alicia has good reason

00:05:21.905 --> 00:05:23.574
to be puzzled
by The Professor's plan.

00:05:23.657 --> 00:05:25.826
One of the great mysteries
of the Bank of Spain heist

00:05:25.909 --> 00:05:28.120
is exactly how the gang
plan to pull off

00:05:28.203 --> 00:05:29.580
their audacious robbery.

00:05:29.663 --> 00:05:31.957
We know for sure that Bogotá
has his smelting crew

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.084
turning the bank's gold
reserves into tiny pellets,

00:05:34.168 --> 00:05:35.502
but that still leaves them

00:05:35.586 --> 00:05:37.546
with thousands
of balls to transport.

00:05:37.629 --> 00:05:39.590
Well, some fans
think The Professor

00:05:39.673 --> 00:05:40.966
has already
explained the plan

00:05:41.049 --> 00:05:43.802
and that he wasn't lying
to Sierra when he told her…

00:05:43.886 --> 00:05:45.971
We're turning it to grit...

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:48.515
into...

00:05:49.516 --> 00:05:51.727
two-millimeter nuggets
to get it out.

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:54.146
It would be bold to tell
your enemy your scheme,

00:05:54.229 --> 00:05:56.773
but he could be relying
on Sierra not believing him,

00:05:56.857 --> 00:05:59.234
which, conveniently,
she doesn't!

00:05:59.318 --> 00:06:01.069
You think I'm stupid, right?

00:06:01.153 --> 00:06:02.446
There are lots
of fan theories

00:06:02.529 --> 00:06:03.864
about the robbers
using water

00:06:03.947 --> 00:06:05.282
to transport
the gold nuggets

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:06.700
out of the Bank of Spain.

00:06:06.783 --> 00:06:08.952
The fact that the main vault
is flooded with water

00:06:09.036 --> 00:06:09.953
as a security measure

00:06:10.037 --> 00:06:12.831
means that water eventually
needs to be flushed out,

00:06:12.915 --> 00:06:15.250
and that could be the key
to removing the gold.

00:06:15.334 --> 00:06:17.461
Other fans think this plan
has been foreshadowed

00:06:17.544 --> 00:06:19.338
in Berlin's
Copenhagen robbery.

00:06:19.421 --> 00:06:21.465
Having removed the Viking
gold from the vault,

00:06:21.548 --> 00:06:23.383
Berlin throws it
into the river

00:06:23.467 --> 00:06:24.760
to the dismay of Rafael.

00:06:25.344 --> 00:06:27.429
But it was all part
of Berlin's master plan,

00:06:28.013 --> 00:06:29.598
as his crew
later collect the gold

00:06:29.681 --> 00:06:31.183
from the water
at a safer time.

00:06:31.767 --> 00:06:33.101
Is this a dry run?

00:06:33.185 --> 00:06:36.230
Well, more of a wet run,
for the Bank of Spain heist?

00:06:36.313 --> 00:06:38.148
The other question is
how to get the team

00:06:38.232 --> 00:06:39.775
out of the bank
with the gold.

00:06:39.858 --> 00:06:42.110
You can't flush Helsinki
down a toilet.

00:06:42.194 --> 00:06:45.030
One fan theory thinks the
plan is to get the gold out

00:06:45.113 --> 00:06:47.199
and then hold it hostage
in exchange for the crew.

00:06:47.282 --> 00:06:48.742
Tamayo tells us
again and again

00:06:48.825 --> 00:06:50.202
how important the gold is.

00:06:50.285 --> 00:06:53.163
The National Reserve
is a country's backbone.

00:06:53.247 --> 00:06:55.707
Is Sierra's dignity
more important

00:06:55.791 --> 00:06:57.835
than the safety of
47 million people?

00:06:57.918 --> 00:07:00.671
If they're so scared of
tanking the Spanish economy,

00:07:00.754 --> 00:07:02.589
surely that's got
to be worth the price

00:07:02.673 --> 00:07:03.882
of a few bank robbers.

00:07:03.966 --> 00:07:06.718
One really out-there
fan theory suggests the gold

00:07:06.802 --> 00:07:08.345
isn't even
the primary target

00:07:08.428 --> 00:07:09.805
in the Bank of Spain heist

00:07:09.888 --> 00:07:12.266
and is a diversion
from the robbers' real goal.

00:07:12.349 --> 00:07:14.643
This theory begins
in the Copenhagen flashback,

00:07:14.726 --> 00:07:16.603
where Berlin
explains to Rafael

00:07:16.687 --> 00:07:18.730
how to pull off
a crime with no risk.

00:07:19.231 --> 00:07:22.776
So tell me, Dad,
what's a zero-risk robbery?

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:25.988
One that goes unnoticed
when you rob them.

00:07:26.071 --> 00:07:28.115
Berlin's plan
to steal Viking gold

00:07:28.198 --> 00:07:30.784
involves replacing priceless
pieces with brass replicas

00:07:30.868 --> 00:07:31.994
so that the museum owners

00:07:32.077 --> 00:07:33.203
won't realise
they've been robbed

00:07:33.287 --> 00:07:34.371
for many months.

00:07:34.454 --> 00:07:36.540
After all, you can't
be accused of a crime

00:07:36.623 --> 00:07:38.000
that no one knows about.

00:07:38.083 --> 00:07:40.085
Jump forward
to the Bank of Spain heist

00:07:40.169 --> 00:07:42.504
and pay close attention
to the bank's museum.

00:07:42.588 --> 00:07:44.006
We hear Denver and Palermo

00:07:44.089 --> 00:07:45.966
discuss the value
of its treasure.

00:07:46.049 --> 00:07:47.926
Why aren't we melting
all this gold?

00:07:48.010 --> 00:07:49.761
This gold
was already stolen one.

00:07:49.845 --> 00:07:51.763
It can't be stolen twice.

00:07:51.847 --> 00:07:53.432
And when the special forces
are preparing

00:07:53.515 --> 00:07:55.517
to blow up the roof
to gain access to the bank,

00:07:55.601 --> 00:07:57.227
Ángel warns them
about damaging

00:07:57.311 --> 00:07:58.228
the treasures within.

00:07:58.312 --> 00:08:01.648
There are Goya paintings and
Quimbaya gold in there...

00:08:01.732 --> 00:08:02.816
This theory believes

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:04.443
that The Professor
knows the special forces

00:08:04.526 --> 00:08:06.028
will have no choice
but to blow the roof

00:08:06.111 --> 00:08:06.945
to enter the bank,

00:08:07.029 --> 00:08:09.156
destroying the paintings
and artifacts,

00:08:09.239 --> 00:08:10.908
which gives him
an opportunity to steal them

00:08:10.991 --> 00:08:12.910
without anyone realising.

00:08:12.993 --> 00:08:14.828
Admittedly,
if this is the plan,

00:08:14.912 --> 00:08:15.996
they've kept it quiet,

00:08:16.079 --> 00:08:18.582
so quiet that Palermo and
Denver don't know about it.

00:08:18.665 --> 00:08:20.751
But, hey, it wouldn't
be the first time

00:08:20.834 --> 00:08:22.628
The Professor
has surprised everyone.

00:08:22.711 --> 00:08:24.963
And those are just some
of the fan theories circling

00:08:25.047 --> 00:08:27.633
one of the most
unpredictable shows around.

00:08:27.716 --> 00:08:29.635
Come on,
did you ever picture Arturo

00:08:29.718 --> 00:08:30.886
with a flamethrower?

00:08:33.514 --> 00:08:35.891
Thought not.
With only a few months to go

00:08:35.974 --> 00:08:37.601
before the second half
of Part 5 drops,

00:08:37.684 --> 00:08:39.144
we've not long to wait.

00:08:39.228 --> 00:08:40.938
But why not help
that time go faster

00:08:41.021 --> 00:08:43.023
by sharing your own
Money Heist theories

00:08:43.106 --> 00:08:44.149
in the comments below

00:08:44.233 --> 00:08:46.276
and subscribing
to Still Watching Netflix

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:49.571
for more features about your
favourite movies and shows.

